            "cue": "goes"
          },
          {
            "icon": "☁️",
            "label": "Lifts drops",
            "cue": "lifts"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Like a feather floating on a breeze?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! A feather drifts down slowly, and cloud drops are even lighter.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🪶",
        "text": "Light like a feather",
        "cue": "feather",
        "sub": "Even lighter!",
        "sub_cue": "lighter"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then why does rain fall out?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Tiny drops bump and join together. They grow bigger and heavier, until the air can't hold them. Then, rain!",
      "board": {
        "type": "lifecycle",
